gm-method: never call a headless-browser-launch library (playwright-core/puppeteer) directly in a standalone script for live-page diagnostics -- route every live check through the browser verb. A standalone script that errors/times out mid-run has no session-lifecycle owner, so it leaks its Chromium process tree; enough leaked processes across a long multi-agent session cause severe GPU/CPU contention that masquerades as a real perf regression (fps crashing 3x+) when the actual code is fine. Diagnose an apparent fps regression by checking live process counts (chrome.exe/node.exe) before trusting the number.